Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 00:12:55 +0000

Old versions of a series stay on the list next to the current one,
and a reader has to open each thread to tell which is live. This
series derives a superseded tag from the list itself, so those threads
can be filtered out by hand with "not tag:superseded". Nothing is
hidden by default.

Patch 1 tags the thread a revised cover letter names on its "Link to
vN: id:<message-id>" line. Run over the list as it stands, it tags 26
threads, 131 messages, all of them older versions of a series.

Patch 2 tags the thread of any message whose closing trailers include
Superseded-by, found with git interpret-trailers. A quoted trailer does
not count. It is for the series no Link line covers, such as one a
different series replaces; seven such threads are listed in "Re:
Supporting status trailers in emails" [1]. Any sender may write it,
and the hook needs git.

The series applies to b/dev@upstream on its own. After it is applied,
one "notmuch new" tags the old threads, since post-new already runs
mail-tag.sh.

I tested each patch against a copy of the notmuch database, running
the hook from each commit. It tags the same threads on a second run.
Trailer detection was checked on four bodies: a closing trailer, one
above a signature, a quoted one, and one followed by more text. The
first two match and the others do not.

base-branch: b/dev@upstream

Changes in v2:
- Drop "notmuch: Hide superseded threads from searches"; superseded
  threads are tagged for manual filtering, not excluded, per "Re:
  Supporting status trailers in emails" [2].
- Base on b/dev@upstream alone; the series no longer needs "[PATCH]
  notmuch: Tag patches reported committed", per "Re: [PATCH 0/3]
  notmuch: Tag superseded series and hide them" [3]. Patch 1 loses
  the committed tag from its comment and tagging batch.
